! 
!
!     180-degree (quadrant 1,4) plane-strain model of thin-wall pipe.
!     1 layer of 3D, 8-node hexes
!
!     Model in X-Y plane
!     Ri = 35.375 in, t = 0.625 in. Pipe center at (0,0,0)
!
!     Double-V weld at top (X=0, Y>35.375) with cap passes on Ri and Ro.
!
!     Material is linear-elastic. Same E, nu for weld and base.
!
!     Uniform nodal temperature field applied on nodes in weld region.
!     Spatially varying, anisotropic coefficients of thermal expansion 
!     (CTEs) in weld & nearby base metal to define an initial strain
!     field (eigenstrain).
!     Non-zero computed stresses mimic welding residual stresses. 
!
!     No cracks in model.
!     
 structure pipe_weld
! 
 material weld  $ linear-elastic
    properties bilinear e 30000 nu 0.3 yld_pt 1.0E+20,
               tan_e 400 
 material pipe  $ linear-elastic
    properties bilinear e 30000 nu 0.3 yld_pt 1.0E+20,
               tan_e 500
! 
 number of nodes 8076 elements 3692
! 
 elements
       1-1164 type l3disop linear material pipe,
                  order 2x2x2 bbar center_output short
    1165-2444 type l3disop linear material pipe,
                  order 2x2x2 bbar center_output short
    2445-3692 type l3disop linear material weld,
                  order 2x2x2 bbar center_output short
! 
* echo off
* input from 'CTEs.inp'
* input from file 'coordinates.inp'
* input from file 'incidences.inp'
*echo on
! 
 blocking  automatic
! 
loading unit
  nodal loads
   1-8076  temperature 1.0
!
 constraints
   all w 0  $ plane-strain
   plane x = 0 symmetry
   1281 v 0
! 
 loading test
  nonlinear
    step 1 unit 1.0
! 
 nonlinear analysis parameters
   solution technique direct sparse
   maximum iterations 5
   minimum iterations 1
   convergence test norm res tol 0.01
   nonconvergent solutions stop
   adaptive on
   batch messages off
   cpu time limit off
   material messages off
   bbar stabilization factor 0.0
   consistent q-matrix off
   time step 1.0e06
   trace solution on
   extrapolate off
!  
 output model flat patran convention text file "model"
! 
 compute displacements for loading test step 1
!
 output wide stresses 1185
 output displacements 1281 5 6115
